WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:04.759
"The Suicide Squad" is, by its very nature,
a violent film.

00:00:04.759 --> 00:00:10.120
The comic books the film is based around center
on a task force composed mostly of supervillains

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:15.660
forced against their will by the cold-hearted
Amanda Waller to take on missions no one in

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.089
their right mind would want to do.

00:00:17.089 --> 00:00:20.589
"I thought you were the crazy one."

00:00:20.589 --> 00:00:22.009
"I am."

00:00:22.009 --> 00:00:26.580
Waller's combatants are criminals, not heroes
— at least not in the traditional sense

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:31.039
— and each of them has an explosive device
implanted at the base of their skulls.

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:36.270
In other words, even if someone from Waller's
Taskforce X were to somehow survive their

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:39.940
mission, there's still a chance Waller might
just pop their head like a grape.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:44.650
James Gunn's latest adaptation of the team
"The Suicide Squad" goes all the way on the

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.950
gruesome and gory nature of the comic book
source material.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:53.570
In fact, the entire opening of the film introduces
us to a new character named Savant, makes

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:58.180
us care about him, connects him with characters
fans already know like Captain Boomerang and

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:02.400
Harley Quinn, only to have Waller blow his
head off when he flees the mission.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.080
In fact, every single character other than
Harley and Rick Flag dies during the opening

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.260
— each death more horrific than the last.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.240
In short: when James Gunn says that there
was a scene from "The Suicide Squad" that

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.361
Warner Bros. thinks went too far when compared
with the entire grisly opening, you know it's

00:01:19.361 --> 00:01:20.420
pretty bad.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.590
So what is the one scene Gunn had to fight
to keep in the film?

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:24.900
"You're supposed to be decisive."

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:28.120
"And I've decided you should eat a big bag
of d---s."

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:32.940
When Rick Flag is captured after the disastrous
first team's beach assault, the second team

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.460
led by Bloodsport is sent on a mission to
save Flag.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:41.100
Waller tells Bloodsport that they are to kill
the dangerous people holding Flag "with extreme

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.909
prejudice," causing Bloodsport and Peacemaker
to go on a competitive, bloody rampage as

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:49.420
they systematically wipe out everyone in the
camp.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.880
There's just one problem — Flag isn't a
prisoner of war.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.200
In fact, he's being cared for by a resistance
force fighting to bring peace and freedom

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:02.530
to the citizens of Corto Maltese — and that's
who Task Force X just killed.

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:03.530
Oops!

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:06.100
It turns out, this was the scene Warner Bros.
balked at.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:10.280
When asked if he got any pushback, Gunn told
Variety, "Yeah, I did."

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:12.810
During an early screening for "The Suicide
Squad," Gunn said,

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:17.160
"There [were] some Warner Bros. execs who
brought up, 'Is this the one place that we

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.160
go too far?'

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.170
I think that's when I added, you know, Amanda
Waller explicitly tells them to go into the

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:27.150
camp and kill everyone, so they are following
her orders, and she is in a way the antagonist

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.430
in the film."

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:31.920
Based on fan reaction, though, it seems that
audiences picked up what Gunn was putting

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.180
down with the scene.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:37.310
While the scene of Bloodsport and Peacemaker
one-upping each other by killing their allies

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:43.150
in the Corto Maltesean resistance is certainly
a shocking and brutally ironic bit of ultraviolence

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:44.900
... that's kind of the point.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:48.630
"The Suicide Squad" is one of those films
where the protagonists aren't necessarily

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.480
the good guys in the grander scheme of things.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.770
A scene like the massacre at the rebel camp
is a way to remind the viewer that while they

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:58.950
may be rooting for these characters in the
moment, there is a whole lot of moral grey

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.460
area to contend with.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.390
At least, that's how fans on Reddit saw it.

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:07.020
In a general discussion thread for the film
on the "Movies" subreddit, several viewers

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.590
shared their thoughts on the controversial
scene.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:12.720
User u/RazorThought instigated the discussion
by writing,

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:17.160
"Favorite scene was when the Squad is infiltrating
the resistance camp and Bloodsport &amp; Peacemaker

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:21.430
are trying to outdo each other with flashy
kills...just to find out they were accidentally

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.430
killing the good guys the whole time.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:24.880
That scene was A+."

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:29.910
User u/kchuyamewtwo agreed, adding that the
scene forces a necessary recalibration in

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:30.910
the viewer's perception.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.030
They wrote,

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:35.209
"Just reminding us that these are villains
of our superheroes.

00:03:35.209 --> 00:03:37.849
Ready to do anything for their personal ambitions."

00:03:37.849 --> 00:03:43.130
For u/Arma104, the scene was also indicative
of the improvements that "The Suicide Squad"

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:47.430
made over the infamous 2016 attempt at bringing
the concept to screen.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.430
They wrote,

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:52.319
"This is what impressed me most about the
movie.The first one was hellbent on trying

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:54.690
to make the characters cool and edgy.

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:59.430
This one they're doing the most vile, evil
s—, and are absolute dorks and morons."

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:01.390
"We're bad guys.

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:03.300
It's what we do."

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:09.159
"The Suicide Squad" is in theaters and streaming
on HBO Max now.

